# 低频词汇 List08
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List08核心词汇

{{conform}}{/kənˈfɔːm/}{遵守；符合}{Products must conform to international quality standards.}}
{{confront}}{/kənˈfrʌnt/}{面对；对抗}{The nation must confront the issue of income inequality.}}
{{congregation}}{/ˌkɒŋɡrɪˈɡeɪʃn/}{聚集；会众}{The congregation gathered for the Sunday service.}}
{{conjunction}}{/kənˈdʒʌŋkʃn/}{连接；连词}{The two events happened in conjunction with each other.}}
{{conquest}}{/ˈkɒŋkwest/}{征服；占领}{The conquest of the mountain took three days.}}
{{conscience}}{/ˈkɒnʃəns/}{良心；道德心}{His conscience would not let him ignore the injustice.}}
{{consecutive}}{/kənˈsekjətɪv/}{连续的；连贯的}{It rained for five consecutive days.}}
{{consensus}}{/kənˈsensəs/}{共识；一致意见}{After much debate, a consensus was finally reached.}}
{{consequent}}{/ˈkɒnsɪkwənt/}{随之发生的；必然的}{The flooding and consequent damage were devastating.}}
{{conserve}}{/kənˈsɜːv/}{保护；节约}{We must conserve water during the drought.}}
{{consolidate}}{/kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt/}{巩固；合并}{The company consolidated its position in the market.}}
{{conspiracy}}{/kənˈspɪrəsi/}{阴谋；共谋}{The conspiracy to defraud investors was uncovered.}}
{{constitute}}{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt/}{构成；设立}{These elements constitute the foundation of the theory.}}
{{contaminate}}{/kənˈtæmɪneɪt/}{污染；弄脏}{Industrial waste contaminated the river water.}}
{{contemplate}}{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/}{沉思；打算}{She sat quietly, contemplating her next move.}}
{{contempt}}{/kənˈtempt/}{蔑视；藐视}{He showed contempt for the rules and regulations.}}
{{contend}}{/kənˈtend/}{竞争；主张}{Several firms contended for the government contract.}}
{{contentious}}{/kənˈtenʃəs/}{有争议的；引起争论的}{The topic remains highly contentious among scholars.}}
{{contingent}}{/kənˈtɪndʒənt/}{取决于；代表团}{Success is contingent upon hard work and dedication.}}
{{contradict}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/}{反驳；与...矛盾}{The witness's statement contradicted the earlier evidence.}}
{{contrary}}{/ˈkɒntrəri/}{相反的；对立的}{Contrary to popular belief, bats are not blind.}}
{{contrast}}{/ˈkɒntrɑːst/}{对比；对照}{In contrast to last year, sales have improved significantly.}}
{{controversy}}{/ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi/}{争论；论战}{The policy change sparked intense controversy.}}
{{convene}}{/kənˈviːn/}{召集；集合}{The board convened an emergency meeting.}}
{{conventional}}{/kənˈvenʃənl/}{传统的；常规的}{Conventional medicine may not work for everyone.}}
{{converge}}{/kənˈvɜːdʒ/}{汇聚；趋同}{The two roads converge at the bridge.}}
{{convict}}{/kənˈvɪkt/}{定罪；罪犯}{The jury convicted the defendant of fraud.}}
{{cooperate}}{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}{合作；配合}{Nations must cooperate to address global challenges.}}
{{coordinate}}{/kəʊˈɔːdɪneɪt/}{协调；配合}{The team needs to coordinate their efforts more effectively.}}
{{copyright}}{/ˈkɒpɪraɪt/}{版权；著作权}{Copyright protects the rights of creators and authors.}}
